    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mullery O’Gara are pleased to present to the market 81 Cook Street. Possibly one of the finest properties to come to market in this locality in recent years. A stunning 2 bedroom red brick home situated in the vibrant Liberties. No. 81 has been full renovated in recent years to exacting standards and comes to the market in immaculate condition throughout. \r\n\r\nWith a wonderful lay out and spacious proportions throughout, this home has been sensitively refurbished by its current owners and features contemporary and stylish interiors.\r\n\r\nThe internal accommodation is laid out over two floors and briefly comprises of entrance hallway with custom mosaic tiled floor with brass inlay. Crittle style door leads to the living room to the front of the property with engineered wood flooring, sealed stove, ceiling coving, centre rose and panelled walls. Crittle double doors segregate the kitchen with a wide range of bespoke overhead and undercounter units by Doran Kitchens with brass detailing, double undermount sink unit finished with a quartz worktop, high spec Miele integrated appliances, under counter and plinth lighting. There is a practical utility room and door to garden off the kitchen. \r\n\r\nUpstairs are two spacious bedrooms, Bedroom 1 is to the rear panelled walls, sliderobes and engineered wood flooring. Bedroom 2 is positioned to the front of the property with engineered wood flooring and storage off. The bright shower room completes the internal accommodation with a tiled floor and walls, vanity whb with storage, shower, w.c all finished with brass detailing. \r\n\r\nOutside, to the rear is a secluded low maintenance courtyard garden laid out with composite decking, outside tap and socket. \r\n\r\nLocated in the heart of Dublin 8, this home enjoys one of the most central residential streets in the city. Grafton Street, Henry Street, and both the Red and Green LUAS lines are all within a 5–15 minute walk, while most of the city’s principal Dublin Bus routes are just a stone’s throw away, providing exceptional connectivity across the city. \r\n\r\nIt is a short stroll from the hustle and bustle that area has to offer with an abundance of local cafes, shops, all major supermarkets, bars and restaurants. \r\n\r\nThe Liberties is also conveniently located close to Trinity College, NCAD, St. James' s Hospital, The Coombe Hospital and the new National Children’s Hospital.\r\n\r\nProperties of this calibre do not come to market in Dublin 8 often therefore viewing is highly recommended!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall \r\nCustom mosaic tiles with brass inlay from Mosiac Assemblers\r\n\r\nLiving \r\nHerringbone engineered wood flooring, wood burning Dik Geurts stove with built-in log store, ceiling coving, centre rose, crittall style door from entrance lobby and Crittall doors to the kitchen. \r\n\r\nKitchen \r\nWide range of overhead and undercounter units by Doran kitchens with soft close and brass handles and knobs. Large panty/larder unit, high spec Miele appliances, extractor fan, double undermount sink unit, undercounter and plinth lighting, ceiling coving and door to garden. \r\n\r\nUtility \r\nPlumbed for washing machine, storage shelving and built in drying racks. \r\n\r\nUpstairs\r\nBedroom 1 (Rear)\r\nHerringbone engineered wood flooring, pannelled walls, mirrored sliderobes. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (Front) \r\nHerringbone engineered wood flooring, storage off. \r\n\r\nBathroom\r\nLarge shower with rainfall and shower attachment, tiled floor and part tiled walls. W.c, vanity whb with storage, radiator, mirrored medicine cabinet and skylight. \r\n\r\nLanding \r\nSolid wood staircase, Herringbone engineered wood flooring, stira to attic. \r\n\r\nOutside \r\nOn street parking to the front with 3 parking permits. Secluded south facing garden to rear with composite decking, outside tap and socket."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "South facing \r\nGFCH – new combi boiler & nest heating system\r\nDouble glazed windows\r\nRenovated to exacting standards \r\nHigh quality finish and spec\r\nOn street parking – 3 permits available \r\nWalking distance to the city centre\r\nBeside numerous colleges and hospitals \r\nConvenient location to Heuston station\r\nWalking distance to local shops and supermarkets\r\nNumerous Bus routes and LUAS closeby"
      },
